# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# There is deliberately NO catch-all "/* /index.html 200" rule here:
# every route is prerendered (see scripts/prerender.mjs), so unknown URLs are
# answered by dist/404.html with a real 404 status instead of 200 + the homepage
# (soft 404s, which Search Console reports against the site as a whole).
#
# Real files (sitemap.xml, robots.txt, assets) are served as-is; <route>/ resolves
# to <route>/index.html and <route> is 308-redirected to <route>/ by Pages, which
# is why every canonical and sitemap URL uses the trailing-slash form.
